name: Pinned scope identity and visible line ranges survive paging, resizing and restart
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NODE_OPTIONS=--import=@REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/deny_provider_transport.mjs KUZUSHI_TEST_DENIED_FETCH_LOG=@ART/denied-fetch.jsonl
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_reader_position.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME prepare
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: scopes
require-live-snap: 25 DRAFT SCOPES · r1 | draft-tree
expect: all: 6 jobs
expect: Tab read
keys: Tab
require-live-snap: 20 SCOPE DETAIL | reader-size-120x36
expect: Control panel client · 1-
keys: Enter a p c Space
require-live-snap: 20 SCOPE DETAIL | reader-owns-input
expect-not: ACCEPTED SCOPES
resize: 160x48
live-snap: reader-size-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: reader-size-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: reader-size-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: reader-size-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: reader-size-40x12
keys: NPage
require-live-snap: 20 Control panel client · 7-12/ | reader-paged-40x12
keys: End
require-live-snap: 20 model requests. | reader-end-40x12
expect: Control panel client ·
keys: Home
require-live-snap: 20 Control panel client · 1-6/ | reader-home-40x12
ask: Across six sizes, does the pinned boundary and line range make position and progress clear while retaining six content rows at 40x12 and keeping planning shortcuts inactive?
keys: Escape
resize: 80x24
keys: Right Down Tab End
require-live-snap: 20 File: apps/control-panel/main.rs · | file-end-80x24
expect: Tab / Esc tree
keys: Escape Left Left Down Tab End
require-live-snap: 20 認証 service | unicode-end-80x24
resize: 40x12
keys: End
require-live-snap: 20 認証 service | unicode-end-40x12
expect: SCOPE DETAIL
ask: Does file reading preserve the exact file identity, and does the long Unicode boundary keep a readable name and complete position range at the document end without broken glyphs?
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 DRAFT SCOPES | tree-origin-return
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_reader_position.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME inspected
ask: Does returning restore the same draft tree without accepting boundaries, starting work or changing source and immutable scope records?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1 NODE_OPTIONS=--import=@REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/deny_provider_transport.mjs KUZUSHI_TEST_DENIED_FETCH_LOG=@ART/denied-fetch.jsonl
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: scopes
require-live-snap: 25 DRAFT SCOPES · r1 | recovered-tree
keys: Down Tab End
require-live-snap: 20 認証 service | recovered-unicode-end
expect: SCOPE DETAIL
expect: Tab / Esc tree
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/scope_reader_position.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME restarted
ask: Does no-color restart keep the pinned Unicode boundary, exact draft and complete source details readable without creating jobs, findings or provider requests?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
